  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 206 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nOverall pattern remains fairly unchanged with upper troughing over \nthe Pacific Northwest and upper ridging from the Southern Plains \nthrough the southeastern US. Meanwhile, what is left of Edouard is \nstill circulating over southeast TX. \n\nStill looking for the upper ridge to amplify through the Plains for \nthe weekend with upper low remaining over the Pacific \nNorthwest. This will keep highs around 100 through the weekend. \nThere are a couple model solutions trying to lift some monsoonal\nenergy across the Southern Rockies and into northern KS for Sun\ninto Sun night. The GFS is currently the most agressive with \nthis scenario. For now will leave mention out but will be \nsomething to keep an eye on. \n\nStill looking for the shortwave over the Pacific Northwest to start \nto lift out Mon and by Tue afternoon will be situated over Southern \nSK/MB. This will push a cold front through the Northern and Central \nPlains and looks to get hung-up over northern/central KS for Tue \nafternoon through Thu morning and may bring some small \nshower/storm chances, with central KS having the better chances.\nAhead of the front, highs on Tue still look to be some of the \nhottest through this forecast package. There is also a chance \nthat the front could bring some slight relief to at least \ncentral KS, knocking highs down into the 90s.",
